@format 1
@id preview.waveform-generation
@title Generate waveform
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Reuse live or stored waveform data when possible; otherwise scan, persist, and publish data only while it still belongs to the active source.
@section I. UI
@tabs Split, Edit, Convert, Audio, Merge, Funnel
@flow TB
@related preview.open-media
@tag waveform
@tag sidecar

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias wave = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LWaveformOrchestrator
@alias scan = Cadroue.Media.LWaveformScanner
@alias sidecar = Cadroue.Media.LSidecarStore

[input] Waveform requested <input>
- Request waveform work after media attachment or display-state change @ flow.PFlowWaveformStart(...)
> valid

[valid] Validate request <decision>
- Reject a disposed orchestrator, missing path, or nonpositive duration and clear current data @ wave.LWaveformStart(...)
? "Request is invalid" > cleared
? "Request is usable" > memory

[memory] Check live in-memory data <decision>
- Re-publish peaks already held for the same source @ wave.LWaveformStart(...)
? "Current source already has peaks" > publish
? "No reusable live data exists" > stored

[stored] Replace work and inspect sidecar <decision>
- Cancel obsolete work, establish the source, and publish an empty interim waveform @ wave.LWaveformStart(...)
- Read stored waveform data from the sidecar @ sidecar.LSidecarWaveformRead(...)
? "Stored waveform matches duration" > apply
? "Stored waveform is absent or stale" > scan

[scan] Scan audio envelope <external>
- Decode and aggregate peaks and RMS values in background work @ scan.LWaveformScan(...)
> scan-result

[scan-result] Evaluate scan <decision>
? "Scan is cancelled or returns no peaks" > unavailable
? "Scan throws" > failed
? "Scan returns usable data" > persist

[persist] Save scanned waveform <storage>
- Save scanned waveform data to the source sidecar @ sidecar.LSidecarWaveformSave(...)
> apply

[apply] Apply source-matched data <decision>
- Reject results that no longer belong to the active source @ wave.LWaveformApply(...)
? "Source is still active" > publish
? "Source changed while work ran" > stale

[publish] Publish waveform <output>
- Notify the timeline and redraw both timeline views @ flow.PFlowWaveformHandle(...)
= The enabled timeline views display waveform data for the active source.

[cleared] Waveform cleared <output>
= Invalid input clears current waveform data and cancels obsolete work.

[unavailable] No waveform available <output>
= The interim empty waveform remains visible after cancellation or an empty scan.

[stale] Stale result discarded <output>
= Data generated for an inactive source is not published.

[failed] Waveform generation failed <error>
- Log the scan or sidecar-save failure @ wave.LWaveformScanStart(...)
= No newly generated waveform is published.
